  "id": "DrugBank_DB00136 - MONDO_313",
  "verbalization": "Calcitriol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hypophosphatemia (disease) through a mechanistic pathway involving Calcifediol. The evidence suggests that Calcitriol, through its indication for Nephrocalcinosis, Renal Osteodystrophy, and Hypercalcemia Disease, leads to the production of Calcifediol, which in turn is associated with Hypophosphatemia. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence scores, with Calcitriol's role in inducing Calcifediol and its subsequent effect on Hypophosphatemia being consistently highlighted across the paths. The core mechanism appears to involve Calcifediol, which may influence phosphate homeostasis, potentially leading to hypophosphatemia. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Calcifediol in mediating the effects of Calcitriol on phosphate metabolism, suggesting a potential therapeutic relationship in the context of hypophosphatemia.",
